  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the first order reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of reactant A gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math> moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> minutes. The half life of the reaction is ...... min. (Round off to the nearest integer).</p><p>[Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>69</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Properties of logarithms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mi>ln</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(Round off to the nearest integer)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "655",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#10230;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mtext>min</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"&#8970;\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>655</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math></p><p>(taking <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>",
